    <statement><p>Find the line integral with respect to arc length 
<m>\displaystyle \int_C (5 x + 6 y) ds</m>, where <m>C</m> is
the line segment in the <m>xy</m>-plane with endpoints <m>P = \left(8,0\right)</m> 
and <m>Q = \left(0,6\right)</m>.</p>
<p>(a) Find a vector parametric equation <m>\vec{r}(t)</m> for the line 
segment <m>C</m> so that points <m>P</m> and <m>Q</m> correspond
to <m>t = 0</m> and <m>t = 1</m>, respectively.</p>
<p><m>\vec{r}(t) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) Using the parametrization in part (a), the line
integral with respect to arc length is</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_C (5 x + 6 y) ds = \int_a^b</m>
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/>
<m>dt</m></p>
<p>with limits of integration 
<m>a =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> and
<m>b =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>(c) Evaluate the line integral with respect to arc length in part (b).</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_C (5 x + 6 y) ds =</m> 
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(8,0\right)+t\mathopen{}\left&lt;-8,6\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(5\mathopen{}\left(8-8t\right)+6\cdot 6t\right)\sqrt{8^{2}+6^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
